type: software

title: "ml-vizkit"
version: "0.0.1"
date-released: "2026-08-15"

authors:
  - family-names: Case
    given-names: Denise M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6165-7389"
    affiliation: "Northwest Missouri State University, USA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/analytics-toolworks/ml-vizkit"
url: "https://github.com/analytics-toolworks/ml-vizkit"
license: MIT

abstract: |
  Reusable visualizations for inspecting, comparing, and explaining trained
  machine-learning models and completed experiments. Provides concise, high-level
  Python functions for common views such as confusion matrices, decision
  boundaries, residual plots, feature importance, and model comparisons. Works
  with already-trained models, predictions, and experiment results from libraries
  such as scikit-learn; it does not train models or make analytical decisions.
  Functions return Matplotlib Axes objects, leaving display and composition to
  the caller.

